# State is JSON

`GameState` survives `JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(s))` and `structuredClone(s)`
unchanged, deep-equal.

That means **no** `Set`, **no** `Map`, **no** `Date`, no class instances, no
`undefined` members. Collections are arrays kept in insertion order;
membership helpers live beside the types.

The shape is frozen at seven keys:

```ts
{ scene, flags, items, journal, refused, rng, seed }
```

There is no eighth key. If something needs to persist and does not fit, it
goes in `flags` under an engine-reserved prefix — that is what
`addObject`/`removeObject` do (`obj+:ash`, `obj-:pool`). If you cannot make
it fit, **stop and say so**; do not widen `GameState` on your own.

The bundle never lives in state. Saves stay small, which is why the API binds
content at construction instead of carrying it around.
